# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE suppression file (issue #772)
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line.
# Each entry MUST include a dated justification comment explaining:
#   1. Why the CVE is suppressed.
#   2. The date the decision was made.
#   3. A review date (≤ 90 days) to re-evaluate.
#
# Example:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
#   # Reason: the vulnerable code path is in a test-only dependency never
#   #          loaded in production.  Review by: YYYY-MM-DD.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No suppressions are active at initial setup.
# Add entries here only after documenting the justification in the linked
# security advisory issue and getting approval from a maintainer.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
